meta {
  name: Quoteless Remote Payment
  seq: 3
}

auth {
  mode: inherit
}

docs {
  Remote payment without a quote (fixed-send), end to end. Self-contained:
  run the whole folder against the peered two-node stack — Setup is
  idempotent (accepts already-exists), so reruns are fine.
  
  The receiver's intent is identified by its URL — no quote step means there
  is no quote response to translate the URL into a local intent id, so Create
  Payment takes `paymentIntentUrl` directly and returns the canonical
  `paymentIntentId`. `debitAmount` is required (nothing else can fix an
  amount) and the payment has no receive amount (`receiveAmount: null`) since
  the receiver's conversion rate is unknown without a quote probe.
}
